    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Capacitance matrix (RHS) with the operand values applied strictly to the node.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="author"><para>Philipp Weis, ETH Zuerich </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
<sect1 id="compare_floats_8h_1contact">
<title>Contact</title><para><ulink url="mailto:philipp.weis@erdw.ethz.ch">philipp.weis@erdw.ethz.ch</ulink></para>
<para>@changes changes Latest Changes</para>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="compare_floats_8h_1motivation">
<title>Motivation</title><para>Calculations with large point source terms and values in the capacitance matrix that can vary over several orders of magnitude require that the material operand has to be evaluated at the node.</para>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="classcsmp_1_1_upwind_control_visitor_1usage">
<title>Usage</title><para>Used within the CVFEM scheme (Weis et al., Geofluids, 2014).</para>
<para><programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">The<sp/>material<sp/>operand<sp/>is<sp/><ref refid="namespacecsmp_1ac76d03a8153fa83afdc1758b9bdc9507" kindref="member">read</ref><sp/>in<sp/>as<sp/>a<sp/>nodal<sp/>vector<sp/>and<sp/>applied<sp/>to<sp/>the<sp/>entries<sp/>of<sp/>that<sp/>respective<sp/>node.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">No<sp/>averaging<sp/>at<sp/>the<sp/>constraint<sp/>points<sp/>is<sp/>performed.</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="classcsmp_1_1_upwind_control_visitor_1dependencies">
<title>Dependencies</title></sect1>
<sect1 id="classcsmp_1_1_upwind_control_visitor_1issues">
<title>Known issues</title></sect1>
<sect1 id="compare_floats_8h_1testing">
<title>Testing</title><para>testing was done in the period before publication in 2014. </para>
</sect1>
    </detaileddescription>
